.env
node_modules/
dist/
.turbo/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.next/

# Terraform: provider binaries and plan/state artifacts. The lock file IS committed.
**/.terraform/
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.binary
tfplan.binary
plan.json
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
tf.plan
plan.txt
# Variable files are per-operator and never checked in. The one value that would
# go in one — `adopt_user_pool` — is decided against (stacks/persistent/import.tf),
# and a checked-in tfvars would make adoption the silent default for CI too: the
# day it drifts, Terraform computes name = "talon-dev" against a state entry named
# "talon-throwaway-spec002" and plans to destroy a pool with users in it. Supply
# it as -var on a human-run plan or not at all.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json

# Backend configuration is per-operator and opt-in: the checked-in default is
# local state, so `terraform init` works on a clean clone before the state bucket
# exists (ARCHITECTURE §9.5a stage 1). Copy backend.tf.example to backend.tf to
# opt in. See infra/terraform/stacks/iam/README.md.
backend.tf
next-env.d.ts

# Playwright MCP scratch output (snapshots, console logs)
.playwright-mcp/
